@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# The mount contract lives with frappe-ui, not in desk
+
+`mountVueIsland` turns a Vue component into an island. It opens the shadow root, adopts the stylesheets, mirrors the host's theme, gives frappe-ui's overlays a portal target inside the root, and returns the `update`/`unmount` handle. It ships in `@framework/ui`, and the app's build compiles it into the island.
+
+## Decision
+
+The contract lives on the frappe-ui side of the boundary, next to the components it hosts.
+
+Every line of it is about Vue and frappe-ui. It calls `createApp`. It provides `portalTargetKey`. It installs a memory router, because frappe-ui components call `useRouter()` unconditionally. Code that reasons about frappe-ui belongs where frappe-ui is a dependency.
+
+Desk's side of the seam stays in desk. The desk loader resolves the name and assembles the desk context. The host loop calls the island's `mount`. Neither touches Vue, so desk's bundle stays what it is.
+
+`@framework/ui/island` also exports `hostKey` and `useHost`. An island reads its host context through the same module that provides it, so no app declares the symbol again.
+
+## Rejected: desk ships the mount contract
+
+Desk's bundle exposes `frappe.ui.mount_vue_island`, and an island calls it off `window`.
+
+Desk would need Vue, vue-router and frappe-ui in its own dependencies to compile it. Every island on the page would run against desk's copies, which is the shared runtime of [0001](0001-an-app-bundles-its-own-island.md) by another route. It also hides the contract from an app's type checker and bundler.
+
+## Rejected: every app writes its own
+
+A shadow root and a `createApp` are twenty lines, so each app could open its own.
+
+The details are not twenty lines. The portal target, the stacking tier over desk's page controls, the theme attribute inside the root, the compiler's comment handling: each was found once, and each fails without a report when wrong. One implementation is the only way the second app gets them for free.
